hadiths[15]{hadithnumber,text}:
"21538","Abu Sa'd Muhammad ibn Muyassar al-Saghani narrated to us, Abu Ja'far al-Razi narrated to us, from al-Rabi' ibn Anas, from Abu al-'Aliyah, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, that the polytheists said to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: O Muhammad, describe to us your Lord. So Allah, Blessed and Exalted, sent down: Say: He is Allah, the One. Allah, the Eternal. He neither begets nor is born. And there is none like unto Him."
"21539","'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Sufyan, from Abu Salamah, from al-Rabi' ibn Anas, from Abu al-'Aliyah, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Give this nation glad tidings of eminence, and elevation, and religion, and victory, and establishment in the earth, and he doubted about the sixth. He said: Whoever among them does a deed of the Hereafter for the world, he will have no share in the Hereafter. Abdullah said: My father said: This Abu Salamah is al-Mughirah ibn Muslim, brother of 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muslim al-Qasmali."
"21540","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Abu Salamah al-Khurasani, from al-Rabi' ibn Anas, from Abu al-'Aliyah, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"21541","Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: And Abu al-Sha'tha' 'Ali ibn al-Hasan al-Wasiti narrated to me, Yahya ibn Yaman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Mughirah al-Sarraj, from al-Rabi' ibn Anas, from Abu al-'Aliyah, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Give this nation glad tidings of eminence, and elevation, and victory, and establishment in the earth. Whoever does a deed of the Hereafter for the world will have no share in the Hereafter. And this is the wording of al-Muqaddami."
"21542","'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, and Abdullah narrated to us, 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to me, 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Rabi' ibn Anas, in his hadith, al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Abu al-'Aliyah, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Give this nation glad tidings of eminence, and victory, and establishment. Whoever among them does a deed of the Hereafter for the world will have no share in the Hereafter."
"21543","'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, and Abdullah narrated to us, 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to me, 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Rabi' ibn Anas, in his hadith, al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Abu al-'Aliyah, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Give this nation glad tidings of eminence, and victory, and establishment. Whoever among them does a deed of the Hereafter for the world will have no share in the Hereafter."
"21544","Abu Yahya Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahim al-Bazzaz narrated to me, Qabisah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu al-'Aliyah, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Give this nation glad tidings of eminence, and establishment in the lands, and victory, and elevation in religion. And whoever among them does a deed of the Hereafter for the world will have no share in the Hereafter."
"21545","Abdullah narrated to us, Rawh ibn 'Abd al-Mu'min al-Muqri' narrated to us, 'Umar ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, Abu Ja'far al-Razi narrated to us, from al-Rabi' ibn Anas, from Abu al-'Aliyah, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, he said: The sun eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed with them. He recited a long surah, then bowed five bowings and two prostrations. Then he stood the second time and recited a long surah, then bowed five bowings and prostrated two prostrations. Then he sat as he was, facing the qiblah, supplicating until its eclipse cleared."
"21546","Abdullah narrated to us, Rawh ibn 'Abd al-Mu'min narrated to us, 'Umar ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, Abu Ja'far al-Razi narrated to us, al-Rabi' ibn Anas narrated to us, from Abu al-'Aliyah, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, that they gathered the Qur'an in masahif in the caliphate of Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him. Men used to write, and Ubayy ibn Ka'b dictated to them. When they reached this verse of Surat Bara'ah: Then they turned away, Allah turned their hearts, because they are a people who do not understand, they thought this was the last of what was sent down of the Qur'an. Ubayy ibn Ka'b said to them: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, made me recite after it two verses: There has come to you a Messenger from among yourselves, grievous to him is what you suffer, eager over you, to the believers kind, merciful, to: And He is the Lord of the Mighty Throne. Then he said: This is the last of what was sent down of the Qur'an. He said: So it was sealed with what it was opened with, with Allah, besides whom there is no god, and it is the saying of Allah, Blessed and Exalted: And We sent no Messenger before you except We revealed to him that there is no god but I, so worship Me."
"21547","Waki' narrated to us, Abu Ja'far narrated to us, from al-Rabi', from Abu al-'Aliyah, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, about His saying, Blessed and Exalted: He is Able to send upon you punishment from above you, the verse. He said: They are four, and all of them are punishment, and all of them will inevitably occur. Two passed after the death of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, by twenty-five years. So they were clothed in factions, and some tasted the might of others. And two will inevitably occur: sinking and stoning."
"21548","Abdullah narrated to us, Rawh ibn 'Abd al-Mu'min narrated to us, 'Umar ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, Abu Ja'far al-Razi narrated to us, al-Rabi' ibn Anas narrated to us, from Abu al-'Aliyah, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, about His saying: Say: He is Able, and he mentioned the like of it. And he said in his hadith: Sinking and pelting."
"21549","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Salih Hadiyyah ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab al-Marwazi narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, 'Isa ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us, from al-Rabi' ibn Anas, from Abu al-'Aliyah, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, he said: On the day of Uhud, sixty-four men of the Ansar were killed, and six of the Muhajirun. The Companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If we have a day like this against the polytheists, we will exceed against them. When the day of the Conquest came, an unknown man said: No Quraysh after today. So the caller of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called out: The black and the white are safe, except so-and-so and so-and-so, people he named. So Allah, Blessed and Exalted, sent down: And if you punish, punish with the like of what you were punished with. And if you are patient, it is better for the patient. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: We will be patient and not punish."
"21550","Abdullah narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Muhammad al-Jarmi narrated to us, who came from Kufah, Abu Numaylah narrated to us, 'Isa ibn 'Ubayd al-Kindi narrated to us, from al-Rabi' ibn Anas, Abu al-'Aliyah narrated to me, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, that on the day of Uhud, sixty-four of the Ansar were afflicted, and six of the Muhajirun, and Hamzah. They mutilated their slain. The Ansar said: If we afflict them one day of time, we will exceed against them. When the day of the conquest of Makkah came, a man among the people, unknown, called out: No Quraysh after today. So Allah, Exalted, sent down upon His Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: And if you punish, punish with the like of what you were punished with, the verse. The Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Refrain from the people."
"21551","Abdullah narrated to us, Hadiyyah ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab and Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, they said: al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, Husayn ibn Waqid informed us, from al-Rabi' ibn Anas, from Abu al-'Aliyah, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b: They call upon none besides Him but females. He said: With every idol is a female jinni."
"21552","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ya'qub al-Zubbali narrated to us, al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, I heard my father narrating from al-Rabi' ibn Anas, from Rufay' Abu al-'Aliyah, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, about the saying of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: And when your Lord took from the children of Adam, from their backs, their offspring, and made them testify against themselves, the verse. He said: He gathered them and made them souls, then formed them, then made them speak, and they spoke. Then He took upon them the covenant and pledge, and made them testify against themselves: Am I not your Lord? He said: I make witness against you the seven heavens and the seven earths, and I make witness against you your father Adam, peace be upon him, lest you say on the Day of Resurrection: We knew not of this. Know that there is no god besides Me, and no lord besides Me, so associate nothing with Me. And I will send to you My messengers to remind you of My covenant and pledge, and I will send down upon you My books. They said: We testify that You are our Lord and our God, we have no lord besides You. So they affirmed that. And He raised Adam over them looking at them. He saw the rich and the poor, and the comely in form, and less than that. He said: Lord, why did You not make Your servants equal? He said: I wanted to be thanked. And he saw the prophets among them like lamps, upon them light. They were singled out with another pledge in message and prophethood, and it is His saying, Exalted: And when We took from the prophets their pledge, to His saying: 'Isa son of Maryam. He was among those souls. So He sent him to Maryam. He narrated from Ubayy that he entered from her mouth."
